1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:01,580
Your muscles don't grow

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:02,610
in the gym.

3
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:04,930
In the gym,

4
00:00:04,950 --> 00:00:06,410
you break them down.

5
00:00:07,410 --> 00:00:08,340
Every hard set

6
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:09,650
sends a signal.

7
00:00:12,390 --> 00:00:14,260
The growth happens after.

8
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:16,200
While you recover,

9
00:00:16,220 --> 00:00:18,290
your body rebuilds the fibres,

10
00:00:18,310 --> 00:00:20,140
a little thicker than before.

11
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:26,160
Three things drive it.

12
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:28,090
Progressive overload.

13
00:00:28,110 --> 00:00:29,860
A little more over time.

14
00:00:30,180 --> 00:00:32,430
Protein, around 1.6 grams

15
00:00:32,450 --> 00:00:33,980
per kilo a day.

16
00:00:34,220 --> 00:00:35,430
And sleep.

17
00:00:36,360 --> 00:00:37,530
Skip recovery,

18
00:00:37,550 --> 00:00:39,650
and you're just collecting damage.

19
00:00:40,950 --> 00:00:41,600
Respect it,

20
00:00:41,620 --> 00:00:43,770
and every session compounds.

21
00:00:46,260 --> 00:00:47,550
Train hard.

22
00:00:47,870 --> 00:00:49,010
Eat enough.

23
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:50,420
Sleep like it's part

24
00:00:50,440 --> 00:00:51,630
of the program.

25
00:00:53,310 --> 00:00:54,720
Because it is.

26
00:00:55,780 --> 00:00:56,690
Growth is built in

27
00:00:56,710 --> 00:00:58,260
the hours you rest.
